sc: an external sheet gone from its file keeps its saved values

Patch 0086 lets the user update links on request and names every
source it cannot read, keeping the saved cells. A plain formula's
reference ('file:///…/[source.fods]S1'!A1) was not covered: when
the file still loads but S1 is renamed or deleted, refreshSrcDocument
cleared the cache, recalculated to #REF! and returned true, so the
update reported success and the saved value was lost (Ely R15.43).

refreshSrcDocument now checks that every sheet a formula reads from
the file is still in it: the sheet names of the external reference
tokens in the cells registered for the file, the sheets a 3D range
spans, every cached sheet that holds cells, and the sheets formulas
looked up. If one is gone it closes the copy, logs the sheet and
returns false; the cache and the cells stay and
UpdateExternalRefLinks names the file. Sheets an XLSX externalLink
only lists hold no cells and no formula reads them; renaming or
removing them still updates.

INDIRECT names its sheet in a string at run time (Ely R20.11): when
it reads a blank cell nothing is cached, and an XLSX keeps no
INDIRECT result. getSingleRefToken and getDoubleRefTokens record the
sheets each formula cell looks up, INDIRECT's included. A cell
starting a new run drops its old record, and a removed or edited
cell drops it too, so only the last run counts. INDIRECT is volatile
and runs on load, so its sheets are known before the user asks. A
sheet the new values name only after the refresh is a recalculated
result, not a failed read.

